    31	## 3. Not guaranteed
    32	
    33	Each of these is a deliberate limit, not a missing feature.
    34	
    35	- **Who submitted the bytes.** An impostor can submit content through the honest service (case f).
    36	- **What the bytes mean**, or that they are true. A contract inside the bytes is the checker's to verify (cases i, i′).
    37	- **That a key was not revoked.** Revocation is not checked (cases e, e′).
    38	- **That the algorithms were still safe** when they signed.
    39	- **Real time without A-UTC.** Without that assumption, only chain order is claimed.
